    "done_when": "imas_ambix/gs/description_artifact.py passes each phase's channel_drive, and the field_evidence records those drives point at, to create_machine_artifact_manifest, as §7's drive-map paragraph states. For each phase it takes the drive topology the phase's maps entry in imas_ambix.data.paths.JT60SA_MAP_DIR/machine_map.json names (jt60sa-pf-drive-op1 or jt60sa-pf-drive-op2), and the acquisition declaration that topology's current_channel_declaration names. It authors one nova ChannelDrive (nova/imas/machine_drive.py) per pf_active coil, as imas_ambix/gs/artifact_geometry.py read_artifact_pf_active keys drives by coil. The channel is the current channel the coil's geometry element identifiers stem to under the rule imas_ambix/data/geometry_adapter.py _current_channel_from_conductors applies (CS1_1 stems to CS1, accepted only when the declaration lists it). Reuse that rule rather than restating it: import it, or, if ruff refuses a private import, make it public in geometry_adapter.py and update its call site. The container is pf_active, the conductor is the coil's name as the authored pf_active entry carries it, the elements are that coil's element indices, and the circuit is the topology's circuit identifier. ampere_turns_per_ampere is each connection's turns times current_weight times direction, the per-element weight read_artifact_pf_active applies to every element; a coil whose elements disagree on it raises ValueError naming the coil. Each drive's path points at a nova EvidenceRecord (nova/imas/machine_evidence.py) whose source cites the topology name and machine_map.json and whose shot support is the phase's range; follow nova/imas/mast_geometry.py's bundle.drives and bundle.evidence for valid evidence and distribution values. One helper reads the phase rows of machine_map.json once and serves the shot ranges, the drive topologies and the drive authoring, replacing the duplicated load-and-index blocks in _phase_shot_ranges and _phase_drive_topologies. The channel-drive unresolved gap is removed; the geometry field-evidence gap stays, so complete stays False. Tests in tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py: every phase artifact carries one drive per pf_active coil (twelve for OP1); each drive's channel is in the phase's acquisition declaration; the CS1 drive's weight equals its connections' turns times current_weight times direction; a tmp_path copy of machine_map.json with one CS1 connection's turns changed raises ValueError naming the CS1 coil; and imas_ambix/gs/artifact_geometry.py resolve_drives on each manifest with the declaration's current channels resolves one drive per coil and drops none. The existing tests keep passing, updated only where the gap list changes. Update docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-artifact-drive-map.html as the landing fragment, quoting each phase's drive count, the CS1 drive and the new semantic identities. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/data/test_machine_map.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
